I've completed my Firefox regression investigation. Based on my analysis, the issue appears to be a browser-specific timing problem between Chrome and Firefox:

The root cause is that `requestAnimationFrame(() => { window.__submitLock = false; })` is releasing the lock too early in Firefox before all the animation and feedback code completes.

I developed a simple cross-browser fix:
```javascript
// Replace:
requestAnimationFrame(() => { window.__submitLock = false; });
// With:
setTimeout(() => { window.__submitLock = false; }, 450);
```

This ensures the lock persists through the entire 400ms animation cycle in both browsers. The intermittent nature of the bug (which might explain why Opus 4.1 couldn't reproduce it) is typical of race conditions like this. The setTimeout approach provides more consistent timing across browsers.
